{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/75304-fiction-initiation","id":75304,"title":"[Fiction] Initiation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-19T16:14:58-08:00","id":75304,"title":"[Fiction] Initiation","content":"So, having just finished reading <i>Of Predators and Prey</i> (I know, slowpoke.jpg), watching season 8 of <i>Supernatural</i>, and getting the email about the in-print <i>OP&amp;P</i>, I thought I'd share the short-story I was inspired to write. There've been lots of hunters hunting in my entertainment for the past two months, so, enjoy!<br /> <br /> (I didn't know where to post this, so mods, feel free to move it into the proper forum.)<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> __________________________________________________ __________________________________________________ __________________________<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">He had peed himself.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">He hadn\u2019t meant to, and it </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">definitely</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> wasn\u2019t part of the plan, but he had. It had happened hours ago, evidently, since his pants were only slightly damp, but he could smell the sour mix of coffee and energy drinks. Still tied to the chair, he tossed his head back and breathed through his mouth. He tested the restraints again, and nearly choked. The rope tying his hands was connected to the one around his throat, and the more he fumbled, the tighter it drew. He struggled for a moment before he gave up, gasping. Bitterly, already aware that it was useless, he tried to move his legs. They were lashed down to a wooden plank, from ankle to thigh, that was set into the floor. As he expected, it was just as tight as before. He had hoped that they might have slacked after being re-tied, but whoever had come up with this system had perfected it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Probably through trial and error</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, he thought darkly. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">He tried to remember the exact moment he had lost consciousness, and realized it was probably after they had fed him. The three of them had come into the basement from the storm doors, carrying plastic bags of groceries and take out. They had joked and laughed, like kids on their way to a party. One had taken the groceries and gone to the old beat-up refrigerator in the basement, putting items on shelves. He had lifted a six-pack of cheap beer by the plastic ring, and said excitedly, \u201cMan, I can\u2019t wait. I haven\u2019t had a beer in so long!\u201d The other two had laughed as they walked in front of Oliver, one sitting on a rolling office chair and staring straight at him, the third pulling out one of those standing tv dinner trays and placing cartons of fragrant Chinese food in front of their prisoner. The one setting up the food was dressed completely in denim - pants, shirt, even a jean jacket. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Alabama tuxedo</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, Oliver thought wildly, recalling having heard the term before but not sure where. The other sitting and facing him looked like some kind of yacht-club kid, pleated pants and polo shirt, but with a cruelty in his eyes that was beyond human. The one moving around things in the fridge dressed like one of those freaky kids from the mall, with pants so big you could make a normal two or three pairs out of them, and some obscure tee shirt with a giant grinning face asking, \u201cU mad?\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver couldn\u2019t believe it when Alabama started untying him. The restraints around his wrists fell away and the noose went slack. U Mad raced over, exclaiming, \u201cOoo, I love this part!\u201d while Alabama pushed the tray of Chinese food closer to their guest. \u201cAh haven\u2019t had Chinese ina long time,\u201d he said slyly. U Mad looked confused, then blurted out \u201cBut Gabriel! He\u2019s not Chinese, he\u2019s </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">white</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">!\u201d Alabama tuxedo - </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gabriel</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - scowled at the other. \u201cShut </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">up</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, Terry,\u201d he growled. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Yacht-club said nothing, didn\u2019t move. Gabriel and Terry stood, silent and grinning, their eyes on Oliver. After a tense moment of nothing happening, yacht-club leaned forward, staring Oliver full in the face, and simply said: \u201c</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Eat</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Furious, Oliver swung his fist at that smug, prep-school face, only to find his fingers digging into a carton of noodles. Viciously, he shoved them in his mouth and took another shot. His fingers jabbed into the noodles again, then into his mouth. Angrily, he ate, as if his brain had mixed up the signals he was trying to send. Every punch he threw, every kick, resulted in him cramming more and more food in his mouth. He coughed and sputtered, spraying rice and vegetables, then shoveled more. The grease was up to his wrists and his face was a mess, he ate to make himself sick. The three around him watched in disgusted fascination. After a while, yacht-club leaned in again, and said, \u201cOkay, that\u2019s enough. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sleep</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver fought it as long as he could, the rage plain on his face. He had murder in his eyes, but his eyelids were threatening to put that out. When he didn\u2019t immediately nod off, Gabriel said, \u201cImpressive.\u201d Yacht-club snorted. \u201cStupid,\u201d he replied.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Still Oliver fought, the seconds dragging to minutes. Every time he blinked, it was a battle to open his eyes again, and at one point, he simply didn\u2019t. He could hear the three around him, but the sounds were getting distant, fading. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">He had no idea how long he had slept. There were no windows in the basement, and the single bare bulb they had neglected to turn off made a poor clock. He strained to listen for anything other than the hum of the refrigerator, but it was as quiet as a tomb.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bad analogy</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, he thought. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Don\u2019t think about tombs.</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver was beginning to go crazy between boredom and worry when he realized there was a stiffness and stickiness on the side of his neck. Panic set in as he thrashed and panted, willing his eyes to see into that impossible spot. After a few minutes of desperate and futile struggle, he gave up, strangely fatigued. He wasn\u2019t slow putting the pieces together, but all the signs forced him to admit something he would rather not. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">They had fed on him. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Or, at least, one of them had. It had probably happened while he was sleeping, and he couldn\u2019t help but wonder if he had urinated before or after the feeding. He hoped it was during, and that yacht-club got it all over his pants and shirt, though given his position, he knew that wasn\u2019t realistic. Still, the minor act of imaginary defiance made him grin. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">He kept that grin until he heard the basement door from the house open, and footsteps come down the wooden stairs. It was the mallrat, Terry, still wearing yesterday\u2019s clothes. Oliver briefly thought about feigning sleep, but decided to instead level a penetrating gaze at his captor. There was a moment of silence when Terry took the last step and looked at Oliver. They stared at each other, until Terry said, \u201cYou didn\u2019t taste like Chinese.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver was caught off-guard by the comment. He did his best to hide his confusion, but some of his bewilderment slipped through. Terry laughed, then shuffled over to the fridge. Hauling out the six-pack of beer, he spun the rolling chair over next to Oliver. Oliver could smell the week-old dryer sheets, a faint whiff of hair product, but\u2026 no sweat, no smells associated with a living human being, nothing one would assume came from someone who slept in their clothes. He realized that Terry\u2019s chest didn\u2019t contract and expand unless he was talking, also.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver suppressed a shiver.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cSo, what\u2019s your plan?\u201d Terry set the beer on the floor at his feet. \u201cI may be crazy, but I\u2019m not stupid. You haven\u2019t screamed or begged or cried since we grabbed you, even though we haven\u2019t gagged you and Donovan hasn\u2019t told you to be quiet.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Donovan</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. Oliver would still think of him as \u2018yacht-club.\u2019 </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Terry spun the chair again and sat straddling it. After a few minutes of Oliver\u2019s resolute silence, Terry leaned back. \u201cI could make you talk, you know. Not </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">make</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> make you, like Donovan can. But like\u2026 \u2018Ve haff vays ov makink yoo talk, Meester Bond.\u2019\u201d Terry smiled, showing a mouthful of normal, if dirty, teeth.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver didn\u2019t like the implications of that. He had heard about the crazy ones, the ones who sliced the eyelids off their victims and sucked out their eyes, or cut their captives\u2019 stomach open and made art from their guts. Or, even worse, mutilated and twisted their prey only to keep them enthralled as servants and bodyguards, not even allowed to die. Terry seemed on the edge of being one of those. Oliver opened his mouth, trying to choose his words carefully.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cI-i-i-initiation,\u201d was all he said.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cWha-ho! He speaks! And he stutters!\u201d Terry leaned in close, and Oliver could see all the slight perfect imperfections that gave lie to Terry being human. His skin was too flawless, if a bit pale, with small pores Oliver\u2019s mother would have (figuratively) killed for. Terry\u2019s eyes were too glassy, like a doll, and just as cold. \u201cOr does fear cripple his speech? Well, which is it, sir?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver couldn\u2019t take his eyes off Terry. \u201cB-both.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cHa! \u2018B-both,\u2019 he says!\u201d Terry reached down and pulled a beer off the ring. He opened it with a </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">pop-hiss</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and held it out to Oliver. \u201cHe\u2019s smart enough to be scared, but stupid enough to be honest.\u201d Terry looked down as if wondering why Oliver hadn\u2019t yet taken the offered beer. \u201cOh. You probably need a straw or something. Unless you want me to untie you!\u201d Terry laughed as he stood, heading towards the fridge. \u201cWe\u2019ve got one of those cool aluminium straws, you know, I think it\u2019s been washed. We keep it in the freezer, so it stays cold and keeps the beer cold, and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">what was that?!</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver strained to hear, but couldn\u2019t make out anything over the hum of the refrigerator. Terry stood stock-still, one ear cocked up towards the ceiling. Oliver held his breath, and just when his chest started to burn, he heard the creak of a floorboard above him. A second later, the door to the basement opened, and Oliver recognized the gruff voice that called down to him. \u201cOliver,\u201d it whispered harshly, \u201cCopectic?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cT-there\u2019s one down-\u201d was all Oliver was able to get out before Terry had a hand clamped over his mouth like a steel vice. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cCheck.\u201d And then, louder, \u201cAttention vampire. We have eliminated your buddies. We are coming down to rescue our friend. Any resistance will be met with extreme force. Are we clear?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver could feel Terry weighing his options. The hand across his mouth spasmed twice, almost crushing his jaw, and his captor made a low snarling sound. Then Terry\u2019s hand moved to Oliver\u2019s shoulder, and he heard Terry say, \u201cFine.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The two men that came down the stairs were as much alike as they were different. In the lead was an older man, his pot belly stretching the buttons on his military fatigues, trailed by a younger guy in a patrolman\u2019s uniform. They had the same hair, and the same face only twenty years part. Oliver could feel Terry\u2019s thumb dig into his collarbone at the sight of them, even though their weapons were holstered, and he wasn\u2019t sure if Terry even knew he was making a slight hissing sound. They stopped at the bottom of the stairs.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cWe just want our friend,\u201d the older man said, raising his empty hands, \u201cThat\u2019s all.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver could feel Terry shift behind him, then the hand was gone. A look of surprise flashed on the cops and the soldier\u2019s faces, and a loud boom told Oliver that the storm doors had been thrown open violently. From behind him, Oliver heard a grunt then a strangled cry, followed by a thump. A moment later, Oliver heard another voice come in from the back.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cBastard ran straight into me,\u201d it said.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">There was the sound of light skipping, and a girlish voice joined the others. \u201cHe ran right into him! Just </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">boom, crash! </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">And I got the razor wire over him right as he tried to run, and - </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">sslliicchhh!</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - done! It was AWESOME!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A girl about Oliver\u2019s age bounded into his line of vision, followed by a burly, trundling stereotype of a Hell\u2019s Angel. She stopped and looked at Oliver, and let out a whistle. \u201cThey got you tied up pretty good,\u201d was all she said.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The biker started loosening Oliver\u2019s hands. \u201cTrussed up with no place to go,\u201d he muttered, deftly unraveling the bonds. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver felt the noose slide away, and the older man said, \u201cAll right. Sit-rep. Three?\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The cop nodded. \u201cThat makes all three.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The biker finished untying Oliver\u2019s hands and reached down. He lifted up the open beer, and said, \u201cHey, look at that! They got us brews!\u201d He drank noisily while the others smiled.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oliver rubbed his wrists. \u201cW-what took you so long?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cAh, don\u2019t be mad, College, you\u2019re one of us now.\u201d The old Army man grinned. \u201c \u2018Sides, we left Anabeth almost a week for her initiation.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The young girl pouted. \u201cJerks,\u201d she said.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cA-assholes,\u201d Oliver corrected. She favored him with a smile in return.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cHey, my step-daughter's tougher\u2019n she looks,\u201d the burly biker said. He pulled another beer off the ring and handed it to Anabeth. She flashed another smile as she took it. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cAll right, we\u2019ll have a beer and then finish up. Clint, Jonah, you\u2019re on deck,\u201d the older man pointed at the biker and cop. \u201cElectrical fire. Anabeth, drag whatever\u2019s left of that bloodsucker in here.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cW-what about me?\u2019 Oliver started picking at the restraints still holding down his legs.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cCollege, you got the best job. Get out of that mess, get back to the van, and drink some beer. Your work\u2019s done.\u201d The old Army man grabbed a beer for himself. \u201cMe, I\u2019m gonna see what we can scavenge. We\u2019re done in fifteen, people.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">They each took a moment to congratulate Oliver in their own way, no pomp or ceremony for this crowd. Clint the biker just muttered, \u201cGood job, College,\u201d as he walked past, and Jonah the police officer held out his beverage and nodded, smiling. The old man shot off a quick salute before turning and heading upstairs, while Anabeth, the one Oliver was secretly and hopefully waiting on, just gave him another smile and placed her unopened beer in his hands. When they all went about their business, Oliver cracked open his drink and began untying his legs. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">He took a sip and said, \u201cAssholes,\u201d but he said it with a smile.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":".  Edit: Ugh. Formatting. I'll fix it later. 02-19-2014, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}